{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98369e91fb0e49b7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes every KServe serving-stack image — the control-plane components\n34\tand the serving data plane — run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters\n35\tusing validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\n36\trequest path. It covers the crypto audit of the images, remediation of every\n37\tnon-validated crypto linkage found, verification on a FIPS-enabled cluster, and\n38\ta gating CI check that prevents regressions.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all KServe serving-stack images (control-plane components and serving\n43\t  data-plane images) to produce a module inventory: every image, every linked\n44\t  cryptographic library, and its FIPS validation status.\n45\t- Remediate every non-validated crypto linkage in the request path: rebuild the\n46\t  affected images against validated cryptographic modules and FIPS-capable\n47\t  toolchains and base images.\n48\t- Rebuild and publish the remediated images through the existing Konflux build\n49\t  pipeline for KServe.\n50\t- Verify serving behavior on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: model deployment\n51\t  and inference requests through the InferenceService request path.\n52\t- Wire a gating CI check that fails any KServe serving-stack build that\n53\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (blocking image-scan step in the\n54\t  build pipeline).\n55\t- Preserve serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters and keep previously released\n56\t  image tags deployable as the rollback path.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A module inventory exists that lists every KServe serving-stack image and\n61\t  each linked cryptographic library with its validation status.\n62\t- An automated scan of the rebuilt images finds no non-validated cryptographic\n63\t  library linked in the request path of any KServe serving-stack image.\n64\t- The remediated images build green in the existing Konflux build pipeline.\n65\t- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, an InferenceService can be deployed and\n66\t  serves inference requests successfully using the remediated images.\n67\t- Serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters is unchanged, and the previously\n68\t  released image tags remain deployable as a rollback path.\n69\t- A gating CI check is wired into the KServe build pipeline and fails any\n70\t  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n75\t  using validated crypto modules — KServe portion.\n76\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the CI FIPS-regression gate for the KServe image\n77\t  surfaces this epic remediates. Bundled because the gate guards the same\n78\t  surfaces and shares the same detection scan as the remediation work —\n79\t  extracting it would duplicate the scan across epics and leave the remediated\n80\t  surfaces unguarded (shared-surface enforcement rule).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb40571d500dae6","agent_id":"a