iew board sign-off and submit it to\n52\t  the external certification laboratory, tracking the submission through lab\n53\t  triage.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The evidence package contains, for every serving-stack image in scope: its\n58\t  module inventory entries, its build attestations, and its FIPS verification\n59\t  test results.\n60\t- Every entry in the package traces to a specific serving-stack image and\n61\t  requirement.\n62\t- The evidence package has been signed off by the security review board,\n63\t  submitted to the external certification laboratory, and the submission has\n64\t  been triaged by the laboratory for review.\n65\t\n66\t## Risks and Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Certification laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months, and\n69\t  review-board cadence is fixed — both are externally controlled and cannot be\n70\t  compressed by engineering effort. They dominate the strategy schedule and\n71\t  are recorded here as schedule risks, not as conditions on this epic's\n72\t  deliverable.\n73\t- The certification outcome and its timing are outside this epic's control;\n74\t  this epic's completion point is the assembled, board-approved, submitted,\n75\t  and lab-triaged evidence package.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-2 (P0): a compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n80\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n81\t  review board to the external certification lab.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb40571d500dae6","agent_id":"adf1730c530c0209a","session_id":"177f2182-dcad-4f2f-b1fd-9c1f9eb2a18a","uuid":"9ef506b6-7e2b-4b03-ae41-e2b2cb23eb68","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:22:01.247Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b75b28c9d15bdc1d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
